The most common use case for OR-combining run conditions that I've seen is to make a system run in multiple states (or other state-like resource type).

For example:

```rust
enum GameMode {
    Singleplayer,
    Multiplayer,
    Tutorial,
}

app.add_system(move_player_units.run_if(
    resource_equals(GameMode::Singleplayer)
        .or_else(resource_equals(GameMode::Multiplayer))
));
app.add_system(move_ai_units.run_if(
    resource_equals(GameMode::Singleplayer)
        .or_else(resource_equals(GameMode::Tutorial))
));
```

You could come up with something along those lines, for the example. It does not seem "contrived" to me. Very much a real-world use-case.
